(7476362, 1187786, 172697, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Neat:</b></div><hr/><i> Congratulations  on your ribbon,  a very colourful image! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you :)<br/> <br/>And to think that I had half an idea to send this in BW!<br/> <br/>Good for me <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=109387" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">alexkc</a> and <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=179608" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">sisto</a> discouraged me to do so :)<br/></td>', 'Originally posted by Neat: Congratulations  on your ribbon,  a very colourful image!   Thank you :) And to think that I had half an idea to send this in BW! Good for me  alexkc and  sisto discouraged me to do so :)', '2016-09-30 05:53:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(7476363, 1188007, 114285, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Waitingsilence:</b></div><hr/><i> When I first saw this I thought the space on the left and bottom and the date 1935 just leaning on the top of the frame were a bit misleading to my eye.<br/>Then I looked at this again and again (yep, at least 2 of those 100+ exceeding views are mine :P ) and I noticed the car and the lady with yet another hat on the left of the print!<br/> <br/>I don''t know if the other hat was intended, but it gives the image a nice touch, just like <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=163081" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">GeorgesBogaert</a> picture''s scooters, given that an italian motorcycles manifacturer makes a scooter whose name is "Typhoon" :D<br/> <br/>So, even though I still think the whole frame might have been moved "up" a bit, I say: well deserved second place :)<br/> <br/>Congrats! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/> Thank you for the honest comment. I too was not comfortable with the close-crop to the top near the 1935 but the backdrop was actually exactly that, a backdrop around a construction site and it ended with the numbers. The crop didn''t look good  any other way. Glad You noticed the lady with the hat,  I was wondering if anyone else would.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2016-10-01 08:00:39.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by Waitingsilence: When I first saw this I thought the space on the left and bottom and the date 1935 just leaning on the top of the frame were a bit misleading to my eye.Then I looked at this again and again (yep, at least 2 of those 100+ exceeding views are mine :P ) and I noticed the car and the lady with yet another hat on the left of the print! I don''t know if the other hat was intended, but it gives the image a nice touch, just like  GeorgesBogaert picture''s scooters, given that an italian motorcycles manifacturer makes a scooter whose name is "Typhoon" :D So, even though I still think the whole frame might have been moved "up" a bit, I say: well deserved second place :) Congrats!    Thank you for the honest comment. I too was not comfortable with the close-crop to the top near the 1935 but the backdrop was actually exactly that, a backdrop around a construction site and it ended with the numbers. The crop didn''t look good  any other way. Glad You noticed the lady with the hat,  I was wondering if anyone else would.', '2016-09-30 06:24:02.000000', '2016-10-01 09:00:39.000000', 0),
