(7476375, 1187786, 172697, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Pascal:</b></div><hr/><i> Great portrait, excellent post-processing.<br/>Congratulations for the score and the yellow! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=17850" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Pascal</a>:)<br/></td>', 'Originally posted by Pascal: Great portrait, excellent post-processing.Congratulations for the score and the yellow!   Thank you  Pascal:)', '2016-09-30 08:35:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(7476378, 1187977, 97225, '<td valign="top">Wonderful image in so many ways. Congrats on the well deserved blue.</td>', 'Wonderful image in so many ways. Congrats on the well deserved blue.', '2016-09-30 09:01:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(7476379, 1187947, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets the challenge well.<br/> <br/>Good candid capture of a moment of ''chilled'' solitude, he appears oblivious of your presence or the camera, true street photography with the challenge brief of a hat filled splendidly. The composition is generally good though I would have preferred a slightly different angle avoiding cropping his feet and excluding the soft focus foreground as you have already commented on yourself. I like the mono presentation with good tones and detail throughout. A good entry Jonathon and well received with your voters too, well done.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that meets the challenge well. Good candid capture of a moment of ''chilled'' solitude, he appears oblivious of your presence or the camera, true street photography with the challenge brief of a hat filled splendidly. The composition is generally good though I would have preferred a slightly different angle avoiding cropping his feet and excluding the soft focus foreground as you have already commented on yourself. I like the mono presentation with good tones and detail throughout. A good entry Jonathon and well received with your voters too, well done.', '2016-09-30 09:03:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(7476380, 1187872, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets the challenge well.<br/> <br/>Your image fills the challenge brief with the hat and the candid street scene, I like your title and comments, indeed I think he must have been reading from a technical manual that just proved too much for her! I''m not sure the passing walker in the background adds more than he distracts I think your timing could have been improved in fact I think a closer image excluding most of the background distraction would probably have helped especially with your chosen title, the two empty chairs would add a further emphasis of his boring story. Nice attempt Marcel</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that meets the challenge well. Your image fills the challenge brief with the hat and the candid street scene, I like your title and comments, indeed I think he must have been reading from a technical manual that just proved too much for her! I''m not sure the passing walker in the background adds more than he distracts I think your timing could have been improved in fact I think a closer image excluding most of the background distraction would probably have helped especially with your chosen title, the two empty chairs would add a further emphasis of his boring story. Nice attempt Marcel', '2016-09-30 09:10:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(7476381, 1187861, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets the challenge well.<br/> <br/>Hello Erin, hope your enjoying DPC? Well you certainly found an interesting character here didn''t you, well spotted! In terms of the challenge it is clearly a street scene and what a hat she is certain to get noticed and get her message across dressed like that, good for her! Although the lighting is quite harsh and contrasty you have managed to retain good detail. Your choice of aperture has isolated her nicely from the soft focus background. Generally a good attempt keep at it Erin.<br/></td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that meets the challenge well. Hello Erin, hope your enjoying DPC? Well you certainly found an interesting character here didn''t you, well spotted! In terms of the challenge it is clearly a street scene and what a hat she is certain to get noticed and get her message across dressed like that, good for her! Although the lighting is quite harsh and contrasty you have managed to retain good detail. Your choice of aperture has isolated her nicely from the soft focus background. Generally a good attempt keep at it Erin.', '2016-09-30 09:17:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(7476382, 1187827, 57447, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by pixelpig:</b></div><hr/><i> ...where a good time was had by all. Nuthin'' like a good Festival to make a gal laugh like a wild thing! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>If you only knew!!!  LOL...her name is JoJo!</td>', 'Originally posted by pixelpig: ...where a good time was had by all. Nuthin'' like a good Festival to make a gal laugh like a wild thing!   If you only knew!!!  LOL...her name is JoJo!', '2016-09-30 09:25:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(7476383, 1187327, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets the challenge well.<br/> <br/>Congratulations on your high score and placing for this great capture. The elements that work are working really well, the man in full stride apparently unaware of the passenger he is carrying, I like it. I also like the motion of the bird flying towards him, and the pigeons at his feet, what a pigeon magnet this man is! I like the ladies humoured observation, what doesn''t work for me is the man on the right with his phone I would have preferred to see it without him. What an amazing coincidence with you and beatabg capturing the same man!</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that meets the challenge well. Congratulations on your high score and placing for this great capture. The elements that work are working really well, the man in full stride apparently unaware of the passenger he is carrying, I like it. I also like the motion of the bird flying towards him, and the pigeons at his feet, what a pigeon magnet this man is! I like the ladies humoured observation, what doesn''t work for me is the man on the right with his phone I would have preferred to see it without him. What an amazing coincidence with you and beatabg capturing the same man!', '2016-09-30 09:28:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(7476385, 1187954, 63218, '<td valign="top">Josh! glad to see your work once again.</td>', 'Josh! glad to see your work once again.', '2016-09-30 10:31:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(7476387, 1187977, 140305, '<td valign="top">Great image Georges! I can''t believe that umbrella is holding out, must be typhoon-proof. Congrats on the well deserved blue!</td>', 'Great image Georges! I can''t believe that umbrella is holding out, must be typhoon-proof. Congrats on the well deserved blue!', '2016-09-30 10:42:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(7476388, 1188007, 140305, '<td valign="top">Love this shot Anita! Well seen. Congrats on the ribbon :)</td>', 'Love this shot Anita! Well seen. Congrats on the ribbon :)', '2016-09-30 10:44:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(7476390, 1187917, 172697, '<td valign="top">For everyone to explicitly know:<br/> <br/>"Via Cappello" litterally means "Hat Street", so there actually are three levels of "hat-titude" here: the real hat worn by the man, the carved hat "worn" by the statue and the conceptual hat, in the street sign.<br/> <br/>Brilliant!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2016-09-30 09:45:33.</i></td>', 'For everyone to explicitly know: "Via Cappello" litterally means "Hat Street", so there actually are three levels of "hat-titude" here: the real hat worn by the man, the carved hat "worn" by the statue and the conceptual hat, in the street sign. Brilliant!', '2016-09-30 10:45:02.000000', '2016-09-30 10:45:33.000000', 0),
