(7476960, 1187786, 172697, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Lydia:</b></div><hr/><i> This is SO fun!<br/> <br/>And... I love your notes about "the story"!<br/> <br/>I think I would have liked it even more in BW... and definitely with less sharpening.<br/> <br/>But, I''m probably in the minority.<br/> <br/>The hat is just... amazingly wonderful!  Ha!<br/> <br/>Well done! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=86447" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Lydia</a> :)<br/> <br/>You mean something like this?<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1188594" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/170000-174999/172697/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1188594.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/170000-174999/172697/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1188594.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/170000-174999/172697/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1188594.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>This was my BW version, but I really wanted this guy to pop out of the screen.<br/>This explains the oversharpening and the color choice! :)<br/> <br/>Thank you for your feedback :)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2016-10-04 05:12:50.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by Lydia: This is SO fun! And... I love your notes about "the story"! I think I would have liked it even more in BW... and definitely with less sharpening. But, I''m probably in the minority. The hat is just... amazingly wonderful!  Ha! Well done!   Thank you  Lydia :) You mean something like this?  This was my BW version, but I really wanted this guy to pop out of the screen.This explains the oversharpening and the color choice! :) Thank you for your feedback :)', '2016-10-04 05:59:58.000000', '2016-10-04 06:12:50.000000', 0),
(7477177, 1188012, 114285, '<td valign="top">You processed this quite well. But I guess you would''ve known it wouldn''t of scored well because it''s not an actual person :)</td>', 'You processed this quite well. But I guess you would''ve known it wouldn''t of scored well because it''s not an actual person :)', '2016-10-05 05:25:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(7477186, 1188012, 62357, '<td valign="top">Susie, I gave this a 3.  It''s not street photography, thus doesn''t meet the challenge.  It would be a good idea to research a bit what the topic is before trying to shoot, it will increase your chance of a better score. Street photography has lots of different definitions, but typically it requires a human and it should be candid.  You commented you couldn''t find volunteers for this challenge, which again suggests you are not too familiar with this genre of photography.<br/> <br/>Otherwise it''s a perfectly competent photograph of a not very interesting architectural detail.</td>', 'Susie, I gave this a 3.  It''s not street photography, thus doesn''t meet the challenge.  It would be a good idea to research a bit what the topic is before trying to shoot, it will increase your chance of a better score. Street photography has lots of different definitions, but typically it requires a human and it should be candid.  You commented you couldn''t find volunteers for this challenge, which again suggests you are not too familiar with this genre of photography. Otherwise it''s a perfectly competent photograph of a not very interesting architectural detail.', '2016-10-05 06:15:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(7477204, 1188012, 163081, '<td valign="top">I gave you a 6 because I really like your framing and processing. As Neat and Salmiakki already said, Street photography- PEOPLE. This is the main reason why your entry was hammered by most.</td>', 'I gave you a 6 because I really like your framing and processing. As Neat and Salmiakki already said, Street photography- PEOPLE. This is the main reason why your entry was hammered by most.', '2016-10-05 10:01:37.000000', NULL, 0),
